the stock market rallied on wednesday  after the federal reserve announced it  will raise interest rates by 0.5 percent  this was widely anticipated by investors  as the central bank is combating surging  inflation  inflation is much too high and we  understand the hardship it is causing  and we're moving expeditiously to bring  it back down  by raising the interest rate it will be  more expensive for people businesses and  banks to borrow money as a result the  expectation is this will cool demands  for goods and services which will bring  prices down as well but this also comes  with the risk of triggering an economic  slowdown following the fed's  announcement the dow jones industrial  average went up over 300 points the s p  500 rose 1 and the nasdaq composite went  up 0.7  this comes after a rough april one of  the worst months on the market since the  onset of the pandemic in march 2020 and  one that saw the nasdaq's worst month  since 2008. this adjustment in the  interest rate is the largest one over  the last two decades signaling the fed  is taking rising inflation seriously  traders expect the fed to continue  raising interest rates in the next few  months current market expectations are  for the rate to hit 3 by the end of 2022  and while alarms over a recession are  not yet ringing loudly there is  recognition from analysts that the risk  of one occurring by 2023 is higher than  usual and that further market volatility  is to be expected  [Music]
 

